WEBVTT

00:00:00.604 --> 00:00:00.944
Thank you.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.460
and

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:19.810
Closed Captioning by Kris Brandhagen. brandhagen.com

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:04.970
See you.

00:03:20.252 --> 00:03:21.972
I was just going to apply for a job.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:25.508
All right, son, but my deputy just went down there with all the men we need.

00:04:40.972 --> 00:04:44.032
Marshal, Marshal, come on, Marshal, come on.

00:04:44.232 --> 00:04:44.652
Who is he?

00:04:44.772 --> 00:04:45.272
Who is he?

00:04:45.352 --> 00:04:45.752
Who is he?

00:04:49.196 --> 00:04:50.836
Boys, get that man. I want him.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.010
Wait a minute. I'll get him. Watch this fella.

00:05:59.116 --> 00:05:59.956
I guess you got me.

00:06:00.444 --> 00:06:03.004
But I wasn't mixed up in that gang. I was trying to help you.

00:06:03.084 --> 00:06:05.104
Why, you darn fool, I knowed it.

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:08.000
I just want to talk to you when you let out.

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:09.828
I got a job for you.

00:06:10.748 --> 00:06:12.168
You need fighting fire is another.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:17.320
Say, I've been looking for a fella that can shoot and ride like you for months.

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:19.344
Think I'm going to let you get away?

00:06:19.616 --> 00:06:20.116
Eh!

00:06:20.252 --> 00:06:21.872
No, sirree, Bob.

00:06:22.428 --> 00:06:23.168
Take a look at that.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:41.960
What's wrong with that?

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:43.300
Nothing, maybe.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:51.880
It might be funny to me that every time this gang organizes a rodeo, their own men win all the fuss prizes.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.990
When it begins to look like an outsider's going to win, he gets sick.

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:58.170
Two or three has even died from it.

00:06:58.760 --> 00:06:59.760
Can't arrest him for that.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.840
All right, come on.

00:07:01.276 --> 00:07:01.876
Maybe not.

00:07:02.524 --> 00:07:06.684
But it's mighty peculiar that when these outsiders fall off

00:07:06.684 --> 00:07:08.844
from them tough broncs suffering from snakebite,

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:09.520
Hmm.

00:07:09.532 --> 00:07:11.032
I tell you, it just ain't natural.

00:07:12.028 --> 00:07:13.808
What do you want me to do, get snakebitten?

00:07:15.612 --> 00:07:19.452
Now, my idea is for you to trail over there and sign up for the rodeo.

00:07:20.284 --> 00:07:23.184
I'll come along after and do some private investigating.

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:25.300
While you work in with the gang.

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:28.092
Of course, you don't have to know me when we get there.

00:07:28.988 --> 00:07:29.908
What do you say to that, son?

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:32.260
Sounds great to me. When do we start?

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.010
Right away.

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:33.890
Fair enough.

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:40.060
The game is getting pretty hot for us.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:44.620
It's near time that the law figured out there's something crooked with this whole Rodeo business and starts investigating.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:47.860
Now I've decided we'll make our next cleanup right here in Dalton.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:49.540
Head for the border before something happens.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:53.660
We'll stick up the next stage from the mines, grab the Rodeo receipts, and clear out.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:54.700
You're right, Spike.

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:58.100
They acted mighty suspicious when that fella died over in Boulder.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:07:59.710
When do we start?

00:08:00.124 --> 00:08:00.964
Tomorrow.

00:08:01.564 --> 00:08:05.284
board the stage down at Sagebrush and give you boys a high sign that the money's a board.

00:08:06.076 --> 00:08:09.036
The woman passenger, the stage crew ain't liable to fight much anyhow.

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:44.840
Meet my new deputy, John Weston.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:46.240
Hi, Weston.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:47.080
How do you do?

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:47.790
Remember?

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.920
I want you to paddle Western over to the shortcut trail,

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:53.600
the one that leads to Dalton.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:55.220
Save him a whole day's journey

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:56.760
instead of going by the way of the desert.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:57.800
Give him a horse.

00:08:58.380 --> 00:08:59.840
I'll see if there's another scent to you.

00:09:00.316 --> 00:09:02.436
Sure thing. You better get going, man, right now.

00:10:33.516 --> 00:10:35.516
The trail starts right out dark at the end of the grill.

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:36.820
Can't get off of it.

00:10:37.708 --> 00:10:40.168
Then you go 14 miles straight through the mountains,

00:10:40.308 --> 00:10:43.708
and it'll drop you right out of the timber on the main stage road that leads the dog.

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:13.640
Howdy, Miss Carter. Going home for the big roundup?

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:14.980
Why, yes. I promised Dad I'd...

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:29.820
be there i bet he'd be mighty glad to see you yeah i'll be glad to see him too pardon me do you

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.000
If I sit on this side

00:11:32.364 --> 00:11:32.664
Right.

00:11:32.908 --> 00:11:34.928
No, certainly not. It's quite all right.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:25.900
Help them.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:26.520
back there.

00:15:20.508 --> 00:15:22.908
Sure got us out of a jam that time, stranger.

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:23.940
Right.

00:15:25.628 --> 00:15:27.388
happen to be going to the Dalton Rodeo, do you?

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:29.000
Yes, I am.

00:15:29.532 --> 00:15:29.832
Bye.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:33.280
us on behind and ride in with us. Thanks, I'll do that.

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:02.850
It was very fun of you to come to our rescue, Mr.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.540
Weston, ma'am. John Weston from Utah.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:07.720
I came over for the Rodeo.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:11.300
I saw your distress signal from the top of the ridge.

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:15.210
When I saw those men riding by, I thought I'd better come down and investigate.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:17.690
My distress signal? It was mine.

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:20.190
Saw the men coming and waved for help.

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:24.310
It's kind of an unusual place to expect help, wasn't it?

00:16:24.570 --> 00:16:26.680
Why, uh, I saw you on the ridge.

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:28.420
Oh, dear.

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:34.700
Are you going to Dalton, ma'am?

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:36.910
Yes, I'm Marjorie Carter.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:40.220
My father is Judge Carter, president of the Catamounts Bank in Dalton.

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:42.150
I want you to meet him when we get there.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:43.440
You want to thank him, too.

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:46.260
You see, the bank had a large shipment of money on this stage.

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:53.880
Yeah, there was about 50 of them after this.

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:57.950
This fellow from Utah comes along single-handed and knocks them all off the horses.

00:16:59.170 --> 00:16:59.970
I've never seen...

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:02.720
Can you tell me when I'll find Weston?

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.210
When in the bank there, Mr. Carter.

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:05.980
Thank you.

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:13.520
Hello, Miss Carter.

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:16.900
This is Mr. Weston, the man who saved us from the bandits.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:18.800
Mr. Weston, my father, Judge Carter.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.760
Mighty fine piece of work, young man.

00:17:21.090 --> 00:17:22.630
I hope you're staying in Dalton.

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:24.540
Yes, I'm going to enter the Rodeo.

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:25.490
That's fine.

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:27.760
Drop me to my office after you get settled.

00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:29.180
I'd like to have a talk with you.

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:29.970
Thank you.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:30.920
Glad to.

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:44.180
Don't blame me if poor man couldn't take care of him.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:44.840
Right.

00:17:45.140 --> 00:17:46.420
He just outsmarted you, that's all.

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:47.320
I don't like the looks of him.

00:17:47.810 --> 00:17:49.930
He came up behind us and took the boys off of their horses.

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:52.100
Say he will enter the rodeo.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:53.790
We're going to have to take care of him.

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:55.530
He's liable to spoil our plans.

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:03.140
Hi, young man.

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:03.900
Hello, Judge.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:04.670
Come in.

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:05.790
Thank you.

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:07.300
Miss Carter?

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:07.900
How do you do?

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:09.020
Sit down.

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:18.650
Justice of the peace of this township, I've been doing a little investigating.

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:23.250
And it appears to me that this Rodeo gang ain't just exactly on the level.

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:28.600
If it ain't, we're going to need all the good men we can get on the side of law and order.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:29.980
Why, it would be...

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:43.280
You mean to say these people have tied up all the money in the valley on a proposition put on by outsiders?

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:45.200
Yes, every cent.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:48.720
They think it'll bring people in prosperity to Dalton.

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:51.540
And they're all mighty proud of this little valley.

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:54.820
That's why I'm offering you the job of Deputy Sheriff.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:59.940
I figure that with a man like you representing us, they...

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.050
They won't dare to pull any of their tricks.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:04.640
Well, I appreciate your confidence in me, Judge,

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:06.900
but I couldn't accept it.

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:08.060
It would interfere with my plans.

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:09.490
Plans?

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:13.640
My plans to enter the Rodeo tomorrow.

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:16.000
I see.

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:18.720
Well, I'm sorry, Ann.

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:20.380
So am I, Judge.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:22.820
Good day, Miss Carter.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:29.900
I said I was talking to the wrong man.

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:32.460
I think he's nice.

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:10.930
It's right here to announce the first annual Jotun Valley Ronda.

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:16.490
Contesting, consisting of riding, roping, and horsemanship.

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:20.830
Featuring Dynamite, the only unridden horse on the race.

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:22.590
Better be careful, son.

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:25.390
A lot of men have lost their lives mixing up with this game.

00:21:26.140 --> 00:21:27.940
Oh, I don't think they'll try anything today.

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:29.980
By tomorrow, I may have this thing...

00:21:30.028 --> 00:21:30.948
figured out for you.

00:21:31.068 --> 00:21:31.608
I hope so.

00:21:32.076 --> 00:21:33.596
I still say you ought to be careful.

00:21:37.036 --> 00:21:38.816
The trick riders, ladies and gentlemen.

00:21:45.804 --> 00:21:47.724
on the program, ladies and gentlemen, will be

00:21:47.724 --> 00:21:48.924
the trick robbing contest.

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:50.880
Featuring Jack Hollister.

00:22:17.244 --> 00:22:20.404
of it, ladies and gentlemen, will be the Roman standing race.

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:47.610
Ladies and gentlemen, we introduce that world-renowned holder of the all-around championship.

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:51.830
Diane Kent for the calf-robing contest. Let her go!

00:23:24.572 --> 00:23:25.292
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:23:27.388 --> 00:23:28.388
Seconds left.

00:24:02.200 --> 00:24:05.050
It was a brave try, hence record still stands.

00:24:05.810 --> 00:24:08.400
However, we have a dark horse with us today.

00:24:08.580 --> 00:24:11.270
A man from Utah will try his luck.

00:24:37.480 --> 00:24:43.120
Good record ladies and gentlemen, the man from Utah roped and tied his cap in 14 seconds flat.

00:25:10.560 --> 00:25:12.720
There's one that got away.

00:25:13.390 --> 00:25:14.700
Better luck next time.

00:25:21.690 --> 00:25:24.030
Three events he's taken today, that guy from Utah.

00:25:24.820 --> 00:25:26.360
He looks like a ringer to me.

00:25:26.800 --> 00:25:28.480
Yeah, we gotta do something about it.

00:25:28.940 --> 00:25:29.980
Now, I don't want to pull anything...

00:25:30.120 --> 00:25:34.590
rough unless we have them. Kent, you take the boys up to the cabin and Dolores will get them up there.

00:25:35.450 --> 00:25:39.190
Just work over him gently. Enough so he'll be out of the running tomorrow.

00:25:39.580 --> 00:25:40.620
Leave that to us.

00:26:08.690 --> 00:26:13.990
Are you ready?

00:26:14.770 --> 00:26:15.370
Where do you lose?

00:26:35.440 --> 00:26:37.440
The guy you met on the stage is in with the gang.

00:26:38.550 --> 00:26:40.490
Play up to her and see what you can find out.

00:26:41.360 --> 00:26:42.380
I'll meet you in the saloon.

00:27:14.940 --> 00:27:27.300
day's events ladies and gentlemen forget tomorrow is the big day oh you were what

00:27:27.300 --> 00:27:29.760
here for well thank you miss carter that means

00:27:32.440 --> 00:27:34.720
I'd like you to come to the house to dinner tonight.

00:27:35.420 --> 00:27:38.100
I told father that maybe we could get you to reconsider his offer.

00:27:38.540 --> 00:27:39.820
He needs somebody like you.

00:27:40.270 --> 00:27:43.590
Oh, Mr. Westwood, it was wonderful the way you win today.

00:27:44.110 --> 00:27:48.150
My brother, he is a big rodeo star also, and he would like to meet you.

00:27:48.700 --> 00:27:50.040
Won't you come now?

00:27:50.700 --> 00:27:59.700
Well, I, uh, yes.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:29.770
uh goodbye miss carter i'll see you tomorrow you boys get out the back way my brother

00:28:30.030 --> 00:28:30.690
Tryin' Kent.

00:28:31.580 --> 00:28:32.280
How do you do, Kent?

00:28:32.750 --> 00:28:35.130
Pleased to have you accept your hospitality, Mr. Weston.

00:28:35.620 --> 00:28:36.060
Sit down.

00:28:36.160 --> 00:28:37.280
Dolores will fix us a drink.

00:28:38.540 --> 00:28:38.860
Thanks.

00:28:39.780 --> 00:28:42.120
Thought you looked out at the show today and thought you were great.

00:28:42.680 --> 00:28:44.540
Well, you did some mighty fine work yourself.

00:28:49.260 --> 00:28:49.640
Oh, thanks.

00:28:49.720 --> 00:28:50.280
I don't drink.

00:28:56.930 --> 00:28:57.570
Who's lookin' at ya?

00:29:11.160 --> 00:29:13.220
Weston, or it's going to be a big day.

00:29:14.640 --> 00:29:16.480
Now then, if you want to throw in with us.

00:30:00.690 --> 00:30:12.900
Hey, Sheriff, a gang just jumped me up at the Spanish woman's house.

00:30:13.730 --> 00:30:16.190
I got a hunch that if you go up there, you can pick up some of the gang

00:30:16.190 --> 00:30:18.350
that were mixed up in that stagecoach holdup yesterday.

00:30:18.840 --> 00:30:22.000
Yeah? Well, you don't look to me like you'd been in any fight.

00:30:22.520 --> 00:30:24.900
You don't get me out of here in no wild goose chase, either.

00:30:25.360 --> 00:30:27.340
I'm staying right here to guard this money.

00:30:27.730 --> 00:30:28.690
Well, suit yourself.

00:30:29.160 --> 00:30:29.620
Oh, Utah.

00:30:30.480 --> 00:30:31.700
I got some prize money for you.

00:30:31.860 --> 00:30:39.340
Some money there, Judge.

00:30:40.610 --> 00:30:41.930
Yes, we're doing pretty well.

00:30:42.600 --> 00:30:45.060
Took in $8,000 today and expect more tomorrow.

00:30:45.880 --> 00:30:48.720
We'll have close to $30,000 in this bank by tomorrow night.

00:30:48.860 --> 00:30:49.900
$30,000?

00:30:50.820 --> 00:30:52.300
Taking an awful chance, aren't you?

00:30:53.190 --> 00:30:55.370
I'm still guarding this bank, young fella.

00:30:56.820 --> 00:30:58.000
Oh, pardon me, Sheriff.

00:30:59.350 --> 00:30:59.790
Thanks, Judge.

00:31:04.670 --> 00:31:05.290
Hello, Miss Carter.

00:31:18.620 --> 00:31:29.620
Hey buddy, young whippersnapper that won most of them events out there today.

00:31:34.200 --> 00:31:36.980
The young fella that won the belt, Cheyenne, last summer.

00:31:37.940 --> 00:31:38.640
My granddad.

00:31:39.510 --> 00:31:40.350
I've been nosing around.

00:31:41.400 --> 00:31:43.800
It is to me like we'll have to get to this fella, Barton.

00:31:44.930 --> 00:31:47.430
After what you've done today, he'll probably be glad to know you.

00:31:48.500 --> 00:31:50.280
Go up to the bar and make a bet on yourself.

00:31:51.000 --> 00:31:51.520
You're lucky up.

00:31:55.320 --> 00:31:56.980
If you can't fix him, I'll have to buy him off.

00:31:57.240 --> 00:31:59.200
If you're wrong, won't work. I'll use my brain.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:01.280
Word has put it over on you twice.

00:32:02.280 --> 00:32:03.360
Fine, but you are.

00:32:05.390 --> 00:32:07.250
You talk words out there. He just came in.

00:32:07.490 --> 00:32:09.710
Fine. I'll take care of him right now.

00:32:14.830 --> 00:32:15.110
Let me.

00:32:16.080 --> 00:32:16.980
Want to place a bet?

00:32:18.980 --> 00:32:20.640
$1,000 on Weston to win.

00:32:28.760 --> 00:32:29.860
He's a one to two favorite.

00:32:30.730 --> 00:32:33.210
That's right, but it's an easy 500.

00:32:33.510 --> 00:32:35.790
Greg Barton, you're Weston, aren't you?

00:32:36.610 --> 00:32:38.860
My name's Barton. I'm head of the Rodeo Committee.

00:32:39.460 --> 00:32:40.640
I'd like to talk to you privately.

00:32:41.670 --> 00:32:42.430
Certainly, Barton.

00:32:53.160 --> 00:32:55.200
...all the case some of my boys had with you.

00:32:55.770 --> 00:32:57.110
They thought you were somebody else.

00:32:57.580 --> 00:32:59.920
They found out their mistake, and they're sure sorry.

00:33:00.800 --> 00:33:01.680
I'd like to have you meet him.

00:33:02.410 --> 00:33:04.550
Fact is, I'd like to have you join up with us, Weston.

00:33:05.180 --> 00:33:08.400
You'll never get into the big money in this game unless you play with a gang.

00:33:09.180 --> 00:33:10.300
I guess you know what I mean.

00:33:10.500 --> 00:33:12.650
It sounds good to me.

00:33:13.340 --> 00:33:16.420
I've always heard you had to be on the inside to be anything.

00:33:17.310 --> 00:33:18.150
What's your proposition?

00:33:18.650 --> 00:33:19.210
Just this.

00:33:19.740 --> 00:33:21.180
Right now, you're a one-to-two favorite.

00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:24.800
That means you're going to win on a $1,000 bet, $500.

00:33:25.860 --> 00:33:29.380
A thing for you to do, so let me place $2,000 for you on Kent at two-to-one.

00:33:30.280 --> 00:33:38.540
And if you should be off form tomorrow and can't win, you stand to make $4,000.

00:33:40.040 --> 00:33:42.440
Now that's a lot better than $500, isn't it?

00:33:42.620 --> 00:33:43.780
I'm afraid you're right.

00:33:43.980 --> 00:33:46.100
That's fine. I'm glad you see it our way.

00:33:47.120 --> 00:33:49.260
Come in the back room. I want you to meet some of the boys.

00:33:58.360 --> 00:33:59.580
And here's what is going up with us.

00:34:00.090 --> 00:34:03.020
I want you all to treat them right. Weston, meet Cheyenne Kent.

00:34:03.540 --> 00:34:05.520
Yeah, I think we met before.

00:34:06.410 --> 00:34:11.370
Oh, Senor Weston, we will see a lot of each other now that we're friends, see?

00:34:11.910 --> 00:34:13.990
